","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8a170bd2bd9644c6ed627f7f3f262a02bbf3c1b1e005e2047d13b87181132491","compact":"171359dfa1d471adad4173b374a33c920362ecb52fe9e69fce3ea6dd2ccdf38f","nasal":"c4ac806afceb117ef9250d7e647845c7bd7adc28624d498c4def3d808760eab0"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":7,"english":"Do you speedily acquaint yourselves with the cause of rejoicing that has arisen of these monkeys on this mournful occasion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.672,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7dd3cf6832dcf3817c06846e253adabfa9b10cbfd201ae1a8db9b042e1f09f0f","compact":"c22315183f4f81e2078ae01f3bb97cc404a34b47cb0e665834895cf3605c55b2","nasal":"9e05ef98e64a222eeb1f552108764df966dff6fcdc4d249e2bc859d79d83a607"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":8,"english":"Thus accosted, they hurriedly mounting up on the wall, surveyed the forces maintained by the high-souled Sugrīva as well as those exalted ones-Raghu's sons-emancipated from their terrific arrowy fetters and arisen (now).","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f036af2f0087c6adc8933cb79be24af07b2d3707f68bb0c2901186a972e3f365","compact":"c0737f8c65f3f2d375a3680b4125dd83f7d045f37f944c568b40f8f80f82ccda","nasal":"6c036f26996f462832d651c4b294e9782c7b85dbcef4f322d17f381736b675af"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":9,"english":"Thus accosted, they hurriedly mounting up on the wall, surveyed the forces maintained by the high-souled Sugrīva as well as those exalted ones-Raghu's sons-emancipated from their terrific arrowy fetters and arisen (now).","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.613,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4324bfc0070644ceb4280356a9e22d04d38a1d68d4c1b36a8f046bed2e40ead6","compact":"3d21b98e7b27198385f24cba51c5ed81ae4e2952ff684b0912bdbb4a955993ec","nasal":"aa22678805d710761882ca2cd799daf05abeebb8eb670869b1cb0e3a7d05f985"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":10,"english":"Thereat, with their hearts wrought up, grimvisaged Rākşasas descending from the wall appeared before the Rākşasa-lord with pale faces.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.576,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a98c8203fea5d4a5e763e82059e2449cb9bc22118967042cb5d8cdb8e4554289","compact":"1348a9aa1e368c6eec4fedc381f7dddb93082110c48adc1634200265f9a1b75f","nasal":"c52fde6126e47a2d12bba0d0215e42a0273b6773840734be5be03134171a180d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":11,"english":"Then with woe-begone faces, those Raksasas, skilled in speech, faithfully informed Rāvana in full of that unfortunate circumstance.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.79,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d7e39dbc3aa52068347f61d425a7122b7307fb81f84ffc757c520759a750e170","compact":"c4ee8e46e6b1c28cdaf02a8cb24403d071ca6ad7c86c6723079aa854affb2040","nasal":"c4ee8e46e6b1c28cdaf02a8cb24403d071ca6ad7c86c6723079aa854affb2040"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":12,"english":"Those brothers-Rāma and Lakşmaņa-who had in battle been bound up in arrowy fetters by Indrajit, and whose arms lay moveless, having been emancipated from the arrowy bonds, are seen in the field of battle; and those ones like to the foremost of elephants in strength, seem like elephants that have snapped their fetters.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"93d37d47780f3aa896902a35dd9811ed9a5ce9e61ed1e775501510b6be240c67","compact":"b4d8ebcb965e8195f64abdef40419329f4e8feaee4da7b17c0d2af90f5e33a60","nasal":"9c198c6291f42b1a6d3947ac13c9b53468516a6b0bbc74bce16678fabde3b78c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":13,"english":"Those brothers-Rāma and Lakşmaņa-who had in battle been bound up in arrowy fetters by Indrajit, and whose arms lay moveless, having been emancipated from the arrowy bonds, are seen in the field of battle; and those ones like to the foremost of elephants in strength, seem like elephants that have snapped their fetters.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.77,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a5fc0974d24427aac77e8103176b76d8f8bf5701537dd0f88889d37782e2631e","compact":"eb931e103b17026a476af012a09b9154ae2b11b04b7969c7b62a53c3ca41f10d","nasal":"9cc15f4d0bb650f497a474a26684a859079ecd105160cc73b0d76edd322b4966"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":14,"english":"Hearing those words of theirs, the exceedingly powerful lord of the Raksasas was wrought up with anxiety and anger, and his countenance lost its complexion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.551,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0918874b634dd203304912108f527e9c09a846ce756ebd51083faeba745f2526","compact":"769c0ee6b14ddb897232af4bade3fcaff5338fe50bf38fa097bcecbe180d990b","nasal":"a6dd6dd40e1298b3a99a8851c34327a34b0b7c53c5a1339adfe13856f5be67ed"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":15,"english":"Indrajit, having routed them in conflict, had bound them by means of irresistible and terrible arrows, resembling venomous serpents, and like to the Sun himself, which had been conferred on (Indrajit) as boons. But if my enemy having actually been bound by the weapons, can have been liberated, all this strength of mine I see placed in peril.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.746,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7696d2d19567c549462ac167574f93782e1adac62f3d87acb2b337b975c5aaaf","compact":"cba9d905417e4f260f47357ce6333d069ed136ebb162f7ae645292a3b9016931","nasal":"7afd3fb9488fd23ccd4f66f1b555adb21bd5beb3b6e419b3966837b4e83c3db7"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":16,"english":"Indrajit, having routed them in conflict, had bound them by means of irresistible and terrible arrows, resembling venomous serpents, and like to the Sun himself, which had been conferred on (Indrajit) as boons. But if my enemy having actually been bound by the weapons, can have been liberated, all this strength of mine I see placed in peril.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7f80fed040a81777ab73caa0703b90f9cc1bf18f513dddc2f3d9e5feca349c31","compact":"d4e900ff6e252581259442f6192fb87fa6b27aac5b1ac3cd1cc81319c0b4ba4e","nasal":"2bb3df54ca39218c91a4588bc6d4fbd0dd371bb5a8e281a9e13f10bff3274959"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":17,"english":"And those shafts resembling Fire in fierceness, which had in battle deprived my foes of their lives, have forsooth been rendered fruitless.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.524,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f8afccc9d770ac865fbfb14f37dc1186f88ca1e94ae48ce8391d675d0c2616b6","compact":"707cb6742e5c328d46c23b5cf43d0d58c2f5b9c0ce846812551d6ab3f71454eb","nasal":"707cb6742e5c328d46c23b5cf43d0d58c2f5b9c0ce846812551d6ab3f71454eb"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":18,"english":"Having said this in high rage Rāvana, sighing like a serpent, addressed a Raksasa, named Dhūmrākṣa, seated in the midst of the Rākşasa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.87,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7f38b00c6074ce895dc6b62b14f1de70d742174b01f9543b4873e6690a3acc42","compact":"cd4f3ec83f7757c2f7bc2933e836a1754f0692e4504c8fdd586a3d6390fa64cb","nasal":"cd8b839e562aeabc1dbc2691bb79f4fc9f5d40a4dc4b3b6998170a2ac791b830"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":19,"english":"O you of dreadful prowess, surrounded by a mighty force, do you march forth to compass the destruction of Rāma along with the monkeys.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.431,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2ab53099fe43ea2ba8db700c2d5cf3c1e4e1815d472bea8556eb234e188547bc","compact":"7afd9a2bd4812860686f29388b0cca47ff66c99784fa8107acd3f9fe61804b08","nasal":"7afd9a2bd4812860686f29388b0cca47ff66c99784fa8107acd3f9fe61804b08"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":20,"english":"Thus accosted by the intelligent lord of the Raksasas, Dhumraksa, turning about, issued out of the abode of the king.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.606,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ff0da92a124b6b0369367ab87108f2f58eef26043d427645a00170ba3d896c54","compact":"387411482a435f255bf09cfaf4e2903726852a89dcbac91afefde06e046fc2ed","nasal":"dff5845b1922cd2a84570ecb03b157b38a89647bc124c93eb9196a787ef3246e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":21,"english":"And speedily sallying forth from the gate of (Ravana's residence, he said to the general of the forces, “Do you speedily move off your forces. why should a warrior linger?”","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.812,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c1f520d0bb6edb8ef8d344e42bd14a5933d4c57f7a866c650abfc007d593b46a","compact":"3a1945246f25dd66ad38fff25dce5ba433540c5b7b3db2fb74ab9d78862533cd","nasal":"3a1945246f25dd66ad38fff25dce5ba433540c5b7b3db2fb74ab9d78862533cd"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-22","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":22,"english":"Hearing Dhumraksa's words, the general of the forces, following them, at the command of Rāvaņa forthwith made the army ready.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.701,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041022","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5a531a512182d646e386bac38bac37768ef0b10b1cdb9faac77c11cd2d5f5488","compact":"88f0b281aa921fad98dfb124942c33992738f5367ee88a1072ca29fe3063cc29","nasal":"88f0b281aa921fad98dfb124942c33992738f5367ee88a1072ca29fe3063cc29"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-23","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":23,"english":"And those powerful and dreadful nightrangers, bursting with high spirits, with bells tied to their arms, set up shouts, and surrounded Dhumraksa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.841,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041023","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fa558881f85c24214221fc49c25f34a872242c095a93e8216351082421c8557d","compact":"bac3efc5834736387eacdd4e9f7c113ca047b8033f1a535d4fa41f4ff85e49be","nasal":"3bf8d369fe81494e67f48e3948b87309b6fce47ad8d93362ef76a653ae0b53e6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-41-24","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":41,"verse":24,"english":"And bearing various weapons in their hands, and wielding darts and clubs, and equipped with maces and bearded darts and rods and iron bludgeons and parighas and bhindipālas and lances and nooses and axes, those terrific Rāks asas sallied out roaring like to clouds.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.774,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-51-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6041024","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c00031cae98795b61c262c5b1f164dc24c360eefd1e0c98dff73be1af66ff04c","compact":"c